  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342163",
      "title": "Using Type Casting",
      "lectureOrder": 511,
      "videoOrder": 453,
      "sourceHash": "deb29ae08103365491bcb4cef62e92b80c9b8ce98dc58d79d0c3d7550c565645",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.11,
          "end": 4.72,
          "en": "I want to start with some extra TypeScript features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.72,
          "end": 6.48,
          "en": "which you can utilize.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.48,
          "end": 8.779,
          "en": "Maybe you saw that when I accessed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.779,
          "end": 12.56,
          "en": "the request body or the request params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.56,
          "end": 14.71,
          "en": "I get auto-completion as long as I",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.71,
          "end": 16.51,
          "en": "work on the request object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.51,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "For example, there I get help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 22,
          "en": "and I can understand that there is a body property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22,
          "end": 24.38,
          "en": "But what I then access on the body itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.38,
          "end": 26.13,
          "en": "is really flexible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.13,
          "end": 27.8,
          "en": "I can access anything there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.8,
          "end": 30.05,
          "en": "because the TypeScript does not understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.05,
          "end": 32.8,
          "en": "what will be in the body of the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.8,
          "end": 34.75,
          "en": "And the same for the params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.75,
          "end": 36.49,
          "en": "You could argue that it should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.49,
          "end": 38.83,
          "en": "to understand what's in it because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 38.83,
          "end": 40.54,
          "en": "we encode it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 40.54,
          "end": 42.53,
          "en": "but that's not how TypeScript works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 42.53,
          "end": 45.48,
          "en": "It's not able to analyze your averacode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 45.48,
          "end": 48.253,
          "en": "to understand what should be in this params object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 50.97,
          "en": "Long story short,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 50.97,
          "end": 53.79,
          "en": "params as well as body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.79,
          "end": 54.97,
          "en": "in the end here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 54.97,
          "end": 57.32,
          "en": "is of type any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 57.32,
          "end": 59.18,
          "en": "That's the type of body and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 59.18,
          "end": 60.89,
          "en": "that's the type of params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 60.89,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "Well, params is actually a params dictionary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 65.3,
          "en": "But that's essentially just an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 65.3,
          "end": 66.58,
          "en": "with key value pairs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 66.58,
          "end": 68.68299999999999,
          "en": "where any keys are allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 69.74,
          "end": 71.8,
          "en": "The problem with that simply is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 71.8,
          "end": 73.62,
          "en": "we don't get the best possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 73.62,
          "end": 75.22,
          "en": "TypeScript support here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 75.22,
          "end": 77.33,
          "en": "If I wrote texts here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 77.33,
          "end": 80.2,
          "en": "nobody would warn me about this mistake.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 80.2,
          "end": 81.55,
          "en": "And we're using TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 81.55,
          "end": 83.99,
          "en": "to avoid mistakes like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 83.99,
          "end": 86.2,
          "en": "Of course TypeScript can't anticipate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 86.2,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "which kind of data we get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 89.45,
          "en": "on incoming requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 89.45,
          "end": 91.33,
          "en": "but we as a developer should know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 91.33,
          "end": 93.17,
          "en": "which kind of data we get there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 93.17,
          "end": 95.75999999999999,
          "en": "We can let TypeScript know about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 95.75999999999999,
          "end": 98.52000000000001,
          "en": "And now to make TypeScript aware of our knowledge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 100.74000000000001,
          "en": "of how a request body should look like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 100.74000000000001,
          "end": 102.89,
          "en": "we can alter this a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 102.89,
          "end": 105.113,
          "en": "We can set the body here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 106.75999999999999,
          "end": 108.97999999999999,
          "en": "equal to request body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 108.97999999999999,
          "end": 111.78999999999999,
          "en": "and then use type conversion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 111.78999999999999,
          "end": 113.37,
          "en": "with the ask keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 117.22999999999999,
          "en": "to convince TypeScript that this is of a certain type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 117.22999999999999,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "And now we can define a type of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 122.17,
          "en": "that reflects how a body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 122.17,
          "end": 124.31,
          "en": "how a request body for this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 124.31,
          "end": 125.34,
          "en": "should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 125.34,
          "end": 126.3,
          "en": "So for example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 128.09,
          "en": "we set this to an object type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 128.09,
          "end": 130.36,
          "en": "where we know that there will be a text property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 130.36,
          "end": 132.22,
          "en": "which would be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 132.22,
          "end": 135.233,
          "en": "And now if we use this new body down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 136.13,
          "end": 137.81,
          "en": "we can access text on that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 137.81,
          "end": 141.4,
          "en": "but if it access texts, I get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 141.4,
          "end": 143.27,
          "en": "Of course we can generalize this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 143.27,
          "end": 144.89,
          "en": "I can extract this type and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 144.89,
          "end": 147.143,
          "en": "create a new type alias up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 148.39,
          "end": 152.583,
          "en": "Request body, set this equal to this object type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 153.61,
          "end": 155.87,
          "en": "and then use this request body type alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 155.87,
          "end": 158.13,
          "en": "for my conversion down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 158.13,
          "end": 162.07,
          "en": "and also in any other places where I expect something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 162.07,
          "end": 164.95,
          "en": "For example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 164.95,
          "end": 167.253,
          "en": "where I expect to get data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 170.13,
          "end": 171.79,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 171.79,
          "end": 174.41,
          "en": "I can utilize this body in all the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 174.41,
          "end": 176.18,
          "en": "where I access request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 176.18,
          "end": 178.13,
          "en": "to get that extra type safety,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 178.13,
          "end": 180.08,
          "en": "and avoid typos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 180.08,
          "end": 182.8,
          "en": "And of course we can do the same with the params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 182.8,
          "end": 185.17,
          "en": "We know how the params will look like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 185.17,
          "end": 189.15,
          "en": "so I could add a type alias here, request params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 189.15,
          "end": 191.31,
          "en": "but with that we could register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 195.6,
          "en": "another object type here on this type alias,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 198.88,
          "en": "and add the todo ID, which is also a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 198.88,
          "end": 201.3,
          "en": "And then we can use the exact same pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 201.3,
          "end": 202.633,
          "en": "on the params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 204.61,
          "end": 207.39,
          "en": "So here I got my params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 207.39,
          "end": 211.44,
          "en": "which is request params as RequestParams,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 213.66,
          "en": "and now I can use params here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 216.45,
          "en": "and again if I now have a lower case I,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 216.45,
          "end": 219.62,
          "en": "for example, I get a warning via TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 219.62,
          "end": 222.9,
          "en": "So now we have this improved TypeScript usage here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 222.9,
          "end": 226.313,
          "en": "And of course we can do the same here for deletion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 228.9,
          "end": 231.7,
          "en": "Now, of course you can define multiple aliases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 231.7,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "for bodies and params",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 234.41,
          "en": "if you have different routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 234.41,
          "end": 236.57999999999998,
          "en": "with different kinds of bodies and params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 236.57999999999998,
          "end": 238.7,
          "en": "Here, I just always happen to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 238.7,
          "end": 240.96,
          "en": "with the same kind of request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 240.96,
          "end": 242.94,
          "en": "and the same kind of request params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 244.43,
          "en": "but you could have multiple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 244.43,
          "end": 247.26,
          "en": "differently named type aliases here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 247.26,
          "end": 249.589,
          "en": "to use this pattern in different routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 249.589,
          "end": 252.46,
          "en": "With that, we improve this code even more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 252.46,
          "end": 256.06,
          "en": "And now, we're really taking advantage of TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 256.06,
          "end": 258.17,
          "en": "to force us, as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 258.17,
          "end": 259.673,
          "en": "to write better code.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
